          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::812a29729d0569843ec91062",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "At the initiation of anti-PD-1 therapy",
            "finding": "Low initial growth rate and low level of favorable bacteria predict non-responders, while a high level of favorable bacteria predicts responders."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::9f9dc46c0fca85bc8c805b82",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "key_findings"
          ],
          "value": {
            "conditions": "Through simulation of bacterial manipulation",
            "finding": "It is possible to promote the response rate to anti-PD-1 by manipulating the gut bacteria composition of non-responders, potentially achieving long-term progression-free survival."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::180cd9e0445370625d26cf5c",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "paper_kind"
          ],
          "value": "theory",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::5b574c8eff2c26db3363b047",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ],
          "value": "The research investigates why only a subset of patients shows durable clinical responses to ICIs despite their high success in some solid metastatic malignancies. Specifically, it seeks to understand the underlying mechanisms by which favorable and unfavorable gut bacteria modulate anti-PD-1 efficacy and to identify predictive markers for treatment response.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::bc2761f49854f8882dead30a",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ],
          "value": "The study focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome and the efficacy of anti-PD-1 immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer treatment, specifically using melanoma patient data as a reference for model calibration. The scope is limited to theoretical modeling and simulation rather than clinical trials or wet-lab experiments.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::013530ac89b265b4772bb2e9",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ],
          "value": "This paper addresses the heterogeneity in patient responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) by exploring how the gut microbiome influences therapeutic outcomes. The authors developed a mathematical model to simulate tumor-immune-gut microbiome interactions. They fitted the dynamics of gut bacteria to clinical data from melanoma patients and generated virtual patient datasets based on survival statistics. The study aimed to identify predictive markers for responders versus non-responders and to evaluate whether manipulating gut bacterial composition could improve response rates. The work provides a computational framework to understand mechanisms that are not fully explained by empirical studies alone.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::be73708f468266ddc0678883",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "These are model-derived predictions fitted to clinical data, not independent prospective validations. The causal link is theoretical within the model structure.",
            "contribution": "Identifies specific microbial characteristics (low/high levels of favorable bacteria, growth rates) as predictive markers for anti-PD-1 response in melanoma patients via modeling.",
            "facet_id": "F1"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::91197f30babbd6c32cdd1a19",
          "source_handle": "P0525",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "The mechanism is simulated; actual biological pathways are not detailed. The claim of achieving long-term progression-free survival is a simulation result, not a clinical observation.",
            "contribution": "Proposes a mechanism where the initial state of favorable bacteria determines therapeutic outcome, and suggests that modifying this state can shift non-responders to responders.",
            "facet_id": "F2"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::b52cf9e1252591b6988e94d5"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch7",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_007\\64c910a3a897b68c48b39fd88d4fd623cb88438f2742fba7317c27a24293bba7\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0525"
        },
        {
